  "rationale": "`assets/skills/habeas-evidence/SKILL.md` is a bundled skill (front matter `name: habeas-evidence`), so it is a site. The final item of its Workflow checklist, step 7, is \"Next: for findings that need code or tests, or requirement text that must change, return to the habeas-requirements skill.\" That names the bundled skill for the follow-on task. `assets/skills/habeas-requirements/SKILL.md` exists as a bundled skill. The other outcomes are not a gap. When no findings remain, or when a finding needs the user, step 5 says to stop and report, which leads to no further task. The requirement says such an outcome needs no skill named. The workflow therefore ends by naming the next skill for the outcome that has a next task.",
